## Project Title

**Online Job Recruitment and Applicant Tracking System**

---

## Purpose

This folder contains the datasets used to develop the Online Job Recruitment and Applicant Tracking System. The data will be used to design, implement, test, and demonstrate the Oracle Database application throughout the project.

---

## Dataset

**Name:** LinkedIn Job Postings Dataset

**Source:** Kaggle

**Dataset Link:**
https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/arshkon/linkedin-job-postings

---

## Dataset Description

The dataset contains real-world recruitment information collected from LinkedIn job postings. It provides realistic employment data that can be used to build and test the recruitment database.

The dataset includes information such as:

- Job Title
- Company Name
- Company Industry
- Job Location
- Employment Type
- Job Description
- Required Skills
- Experience Level
- Salary (where available)

---

## Purpose of Using This Dataset

The dataset will be used to:

- Design the database tables.
- Perform database normalization.
- Populate Oracle tables with sample data.
- Test SQL queries.
- Develop PL/SQL procedures, functions, triggers, and packages.
- Generate reports and analytics.

---

## Data Preparation

Before importing the dataset into Oracle Database, the following steps will be performed:

- Remove duplicate records.
- Handle missing values where necessary.
- Standardize field names.
- Normalize the data into related tables.
- Verify data quality before testing.

---

## Planned Database Tables

The dataset will support the following database tables:

- Employers
- Applicants
- Jobs
- Applications
- Interviews
- Skills
- Departments
- Notifications

